the sales contract for the house he bought in 1957, my late mother's violin dating to her years in high school, and all my and my brother's elementary school report cards. These are things that made sense from a sentimental viewpoint, and they didn't take up a lot of space. But what about people who save huge quantities of things with no apparent value that have no sentimental meaning, and in the eyes of most people, will be trash? Can saving too much stuff be pathological? Where is the line between being a messy housekeeper and having a hoarding disorder? What drives some people to save enormous quantities of indiscriminate things. And is such behavior merely a manifestation of something like obsessive compulsive disorder or is it a discrete mental illness? Welcome to Speaking of Psychology,

4
